    {
      "title": "TEST PROCEDURE",
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "key": "test_procedure",
          "label": "Test Procedure",
          "default": "The test procedure was in accordance with <Standard name>.\n\nThe EUT was tested in a Semi-Anechoic chamber. The EUT was placed on non-conductive table/ insulation support of 0.8/0.1m height which was in turn placed on turn table to enable 0° to 360° rotation at 90° step as per standard. RF absorbers were placed on the floor between the transmitting antenna and the EUT.\n\nThe distance between the edge of the EUT and receiving antenna was 3m. Pre-calibrated RF field strength level was transmitted using appropriate antenna in both horizontal and vertical polarization. The RF signal was amplitude modulated to 80% depth with 1 kHz sine wave as per standard. During the test, performance of the EUT was monitored as per the criteria specified in the standard."
        }
      ]
    },
